# Vendored FunctionStore helper library inside the companion utility.
# Embody tracks these DATs (the .tdn references them via file+syncfile, so the
# files MUST exist on disk or a TDN reconstruct rebuilds them empty), but the
# code is third-party and has never been version-controlled here. Ignore the
# files rather than untagging the ops -- untagging strips the file refs from
# the .tdn and the content then survives only in the .toe.
/utility/TDXLauncherUtility/ExtUtils/
/utility/TDXLauncherUtility/FNS_About/
# Editor stubs ExtUtils' stub tool generates for that same vendored library.
/utility/typings/

# Vercel CLI link
/.vercel
utility/TDXLPP.*.toe

# macOS icon work. scripts/build-macos-icons.py needs exactly three inputs --
# the layered assets/TDXLU.icon document, the Default export it cuts the .icns
# from, and assets/icon_default_mono.png -- so those stay tracked along with
# everything it writes into src-tauri/icons/. Every other appearance export is
# a preview of what macOS composites itself from the compiled catalog, and the
# loose assets/macos-iOS-*.png at the top of assets/ are a superseded copy of
# the same set.
assets/macos Exports/*
!assets/macos Exports/macos-iOS-Default-1024x1024@1x.png
assets/macos-iOS-*.png

